<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">gmcp-tutorial</ansi>

The <ansi fg="white-bold">Tutorial</ansi> payload is your place in the tutorial course: the same stage, goal, checklist, and hints that <ansi fg="command">tutorial</ansi> shows, in plain text. It is sent only to you, and only when something changes: at login and copyover, when a lesson is passed, after a command, or at most once a round. The web client can also ask for it (<ansi fg="white-bold">!!GMCP(Tutorial)</ansi>). An empty object means you aren't in the course.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Tutorial</ansi>

  <ansi fg="cyan">active</ansi>     <ansi fg="red">boolean</ansi> - true while you are in the course
  <ansi fg="cyan">stage</ansi>      <ansi fg="yellow">number</ansi>  - The current lesson, from 1
  <ansi fg="cyan">stages</ansi>     <ansi fg="yellow">number</ansi>  - How many lessons there are
  <ansi fg="cyan">id</ansi>         <ansi fg="green">string</ansi>  - The lesson's id: "character", "company", "formation", ...
  <ansi fg="cyan">title</ansi>      <ansi fg="green">string</ansi>  - The lesson's title
  <ansi fg="cyan">goal</ansi>       <ansi fg="green">string</ansi>  - What passes it
  <ansi fg="cyan">checklist</ansi>  <ansi fg="magenta">array</ansi>   - Each item has a label and done (true or false)
  <ansi fg="cyan">hints</ansi>      <ansi fg="magenta">array</ansi>   - What to try, one line each

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help gmcp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tutorial</ansi>
